   "source": [
    "-ML is the subest of aritifical intelligence that enables systems to learn from data.\n",
    "-historical data set is used to learn the patterns and predict the future.\n",
    "-TYPES:\n",
    "1.Supervised learning:- labled data which has hidden patterns ,ex-classfication,regression.\n",
    "2.Unsupervised learning:- it has unlabled data that means it dosent have hidden patterns but it has cluster which is the collection of similar data types.\n",
    "3.Reinforcement learning:- (widely used these days) when we perfrom using hit and trial method to maximize rewards. ex-games , finance fields, etc."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "78602c0c-9c48-4ac8-8e4f-69467d87e9cc",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "___SUPERVISED LEARNING:-\n",
    "- model is trained using labled data.\n",
    "- ex: image classsification, spam detection.\n",
    "- common algorithms : Linear regression, decisiom trees, support vector machines.\n",
    "- target - the feature we are trying to achive to predict.\n",
    "- PARTS:\n",
    "1.classification- it has target as binary way it is going to be multi class as well. (the feature will be as yes/no.)\n",
    "2.regression- target columns is completely continuous in nature ."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "d10d8324-a8fa-4abc-9a1f-cb0789199118",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "__UNSUPERVISED LEARNING:-\n",
    "- model learns from data without labels.\n",
    "- ex: customer segmentation ,anomaly detection.\n",
    "- common algorithms : k means clustering, hierarchical clustering."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "8e36f8d9-6c02-44d9-834b-d0afde9ffe87",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "__REINFORCEMENT LEARNING:-\n",
    "- models learns to make decisions by taking actions in an environemnt to maximize cumulative reward.\n",
    "- ex: game playing (like Alpha Go), robotics.\n",
    "- key concepts: agent, environment, actions, rewards.\n",
    "- we dont have any specifics data for it as it is performed at industrial level."
   ]
